text:
{
  "verdict": "allowed",
  "section": "27",
  "quote": "A landlord or, with the written authorization of a landlord, a broker or salesperson registered under the Trust in Real Estate Services Act, 2002, may enter a rental unit in accordance with written notice given to the tenant at least 24 hours before the time of entry to allow a potential purchaser to view the rental unit.",
  "reason": "Subsections 27(2) and 27(3) expressly permit a landlord to enter a rental unit to allow a potential purchaser to view it upon giving at least 24 hours written notice specifying the reason, day, and a time of entry between 8 a.m. and 8 p.m. Because the clause follows all of these statutory requirements, it is consistent with the Act and allowed."
}

